        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Fixing explanations of onsuccess/onerror listeners for IndexedDB]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40025</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40025"/>
        <updated>2025-06-22T17:56:29.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112726619?u=6d16930d0e2054b2b458c320f6f8b85b602b8da2&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">The paragraph that aimed to be fixed contained 2 issues:</p>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto">Logical error: there is no 'success'/'error' events on  DOM event type property, according to official specification <a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2" rel="nofollow">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2</a></p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto">The explanation text was just hard to read and focus, so it is a bit simplified and more concised</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">I made this change, so the developers do not be confused with unexpected 'error' / 'success' DOM event types</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2" rel="nofollow">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2</a></p>]]></content>
